 "explanation": "Tempester n°56: Edit > Copy Sound also copies the sequence, the Note FX and the mixer of the sound, to any beat (Main 1.5.0.2). Forum request n°7 (« requested a gazillion times »), Docs/analyses/feature-copy-divisions.md. Before: Edit > Copy Sound (Erase + Copy, « Copy Sound », Copy Now) copied only the sound program, between any two beats ([routine] [address], the call at [address]); the sequence, the Note FX and the mixer of a sound could only be copied inside the current beat, by holding Copy and tapping two pads, where the Copy screen's soft knobs choose what goes with the copy (Sound / Seq / NoteFX / Mixer: ctx+0x3e / +0x40 / +0x42 / +0x44, ctx = [address]). After: Copy Now also obeys the Copy screen's Seq / NoteFX / Mixer switches: with Seq On it copies the source sound's sequence over the destination sound's ([routine] [address], whose free slot is searched in the target beat since n°10), with NoteFX On its Note FX ([routine] [address]), with Mixer On its mixer settings ([routine] [address]): the routines and the order of the Copy-held pad copy ([address]-[address]), between any two beats. The sound itself is always copied, as before. All three Off (their state at power-on): byte for byte the old Copy Sound. Same beat and same sound: only the sound, as before ([routine] would erase the sequence and copy nothing). The screen says what goes with the copy: the caption « Dest Sound (Replaces) » becomes « Dest: Sound+Seq », « Dest: Snd+Seq+NoteFX »... (seven captions, CAPTION, the string pointer loaded at [address]), no new field or gesture. (Caption wording and 0xFF padding chosen so that no 8 bytes of them repeat DSI's strings: tools/dsi_content_guard.py.) Allowed while the sequencer plays (author, 12/11/2026), as the Copy-held copy already is: the copy erases the target sound's events then refills them step by step while Timer 4 reads the beat. Simulated with the real Timer 4 taken between instructions of the copy (tools/sim_copy_divisions.py, section 56T): no fault, the copy's stores only in the target sound's events and sound record, every other sound played as without the copy; the target sound alone, during the copy (a few ms), plays only the steps already copied (some of its notes of that pass missing). The events beyond the target beat's length are copied too (all 384 steps, as the beat file keeps them): silent until the beat is made longer, as for a beat shortened by hand. Context: main loop (UI), outside interrupts. No RAM of its own (the switches are DSI's ctx bytes), stack 0x28 and 0x10 bytes. Free flash 0x9D079A00-0x9D079B7F (code) and 0x9D079B80-0x9D079C33 (caption offsets and captions).",
